Scribbet — Third-Party Notices
=================================

Scribbet itself is MIT licensed; see LICENSE. It also redistributes the
open-source components listed below, whose licences require their copyright
notices to travel with the binary. This file is that notice.

Two things it does not cover, deliberately:

  * The speech-to-text model is not redistributed. It is downloaded from
    Hugging Face during first-run onboarding, over a checksum-pinned request.
  * The Silero VAD model (crates/vad/models/silero_vad.onnx) IS embedded in
    the binary. It comes from the snakers4/silero-vad project and is MIT
    licensed; its notice is included with the MIT section below.

